+section('agent-setup', 'Agent setup', 'terminal')
  p.
    The Agent (#[code thub]) is a stateless Node.js CLI. Install it wherever jobs are submitted from:
    a developer machine (macOS, Linux or Windows with Node.js 20+) or a CI runner.

  h3.h6 Install
  +code('Developer machine').
    npm i -g @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-agent
    thub --version
  p.small.
    In CI you don't need a global install: #[code npx -y @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-agent run …].

  h3.h6 Get a token
  p.small.
    An admin registers an agent on #[a(href="/admin/agents") Agents] (or with #[code thub-admin agent add]) and passes you
    its token, which is shown only once. The agent's #[strong kind] decides the job id prefix, the default priority and which jobs it can see:
  table.table.table-sm.small.w-auto
    thead
      tr
        th Kind
        th For
        th Job ids
        th Default priority
        th Can see
    tbody
      tr
        td: code ci
        td Pipelines
        td: code A-00001…
        td 50
        td every job (details, log)
      tr
        td: code cli
        td Developers
        td: code M-00001…
        td 60 (so a busy pipeline doesn't starve them)
        td only the jobs it submitted

  h3.h6 Configure
  +code('Save the settings once').
    thub config set url   #{coordinatorUrl}
    thub config set token agt_…
    thub config set user  "Your Name"      # optional: job owner label
    thub config set group &lt;groupId>       # optional: default --group
  p.small.
    These are saved in #[code ~/.config/thub/agent.json]. Order of precedence: flags (#[code --url], #[code --token]) →
    environment → config file.
  table.table.table-sm.small
    thead
      tr
        th Variable
        th Meaning
    tbody
      tr
        td: code THUB_URL
        td Coordinator URL, e.g. #[code #{coordinatorUrl}]
      tr
        td: code THUB_TOKEN
        td Agent token. Keep it in your CI's secret store.
      tr
        td: code THUB_GROUP
        td Default #[code --group]
      tr
        td: code THUB_USER
        td Default #[code --user]
      tr
        td: code THUB_NO_SELF_UPDATE=1
        td Don't install admin-requested Agent updates on this machine
  +code('Check the connection').
    thub resources          # lists the Clients and their status
    thub jobs --mine        # your recent jobs
  p.small.mb-0.
    When an admin requests an Agent update, the next #[code thub] command installs it and then runs on
    the new version. If it can't install (e.g. no permission in CI), it prints the manual command and
    carries on with the current version.
